{"id": "ms-cascade", "name": "Stable Cascade cosine + shift", "family": "scheduler", "subfamily": "core-model-sampling", "plain": "Cosine \u1fb1 schedule with a logSNR shift, used by Stable Cascade. The sigma table is present only so other schedulers work. \u1fb1 is clamped so sigma cannot run to infinity or zero.", "math": "\u1fb1(t)=cos\u00b2((t+s)/(1+s)\u00b7\u03c0/2)/cos\u00b2(s/(1+s)\u00b7\u03c0/2), s=0.008.\nIf shift\u22601: logSNR += 2\u00b7ln(1/shift); \u1fb1=sigmoid(logSNR).\n\u1fb1 clamped to [1e-4, 0.9999]. \u03c3=\u221a((1\u2212\u1fb1)/\u1fb1). Table has 10000 entries.", "props": {"shape": "cosine \u1fb1 with logSNR shift", "params": "shift=2.0 (node default)", "needs_model_sampling": true}, "evidence": [{"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/model_sampling.py:359", "symbol": "StableCascadeSampling"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy_extras/nodes_model_advanced.py:94", "symbol": "ModelSamplingStableCascade"}], "providers": [{"pack": "core", "author": "Comfy Org and contributors", "licence": "GPL-3.0", "kind": "original", "nodes": ["ModelSamplingStableCascade"], "note": "", "verdict": "", "risks": [], "res4lyf": false}], "providers_n": 1, "in_core": true, "live": false, "needs_pack": false, "core_ref": {"node": "ModelSamplingStableCascade"}, "family_fit": [{"family": "Stable Cascade", "why": "stage C default shift 2.0, stage B 1.0", "label": "from code", "source": "ComfyUI/comfy/supported_models.py:444"}], "claims": [], "label": "from code", "surprise": "", "rendered": false, "rendered_ids": [], "risks": [], "flagged_providers": 0, "licences": ["GPL-3.0"], "verdicts": [], "audit": {"verdict": "correct", "fixed": false, "note": ""}, "run_patch": "", "run_guider": "", "prefer_model": ""}